brings together the  heroes and villains of each story into  one superhero universe but it gets even  wilder from there it turns out that  Kevin Wendell crumb aka the hoard and  David Dunn aka bee overseer are not the  most powerful forces in their world as  their final clash is underway Shyamalan  reveals that they were brought together  not to be studied or have their  superpowers revealed but to be executed  by a secret society determined  keep the balance by wiping out gifted  people then of course Shyamalan couldn't  help but throw in another twist by  making the brilliant mr. glass construct  a counter scheme that resulted in proof  of superheroes being released to the  world establishing the potential for an  even bigger universe and presumably even  more twists to come Avengers endgame was  only ever going to end one way with the  Avengers finding a path to defeating  Thanos and restoring their snapped out  friends to life after the events of  infinity war we knew that going in the  only mystery was in how it would happen  and the film through viewers for a loop  just a few minutes into the adventure  the stage is set for an Avengers vs.  Thanos rematch almost right away but  when the surviving members of Earth's  Mightiest Heroes get to him Thanos  reveals that he's already destroyed the  Infinity stones they used the stones to  destroy the stones but the work is done  Thor executes Stano said before we can  even get over the shock of that death  the film jumps ahead five years to show  a seemingly dude world the 2019 film  adaptation of Stephen King's Pet  Sematary didn't attempt to hide its  major alterations to the source material  some of the film's earliest trailers  gave a way that the new movie was going  to make the Creed families eldest child  Ellie the victim of a tragic early death  and even more tragic resurrection that  runs contrary to King's book which kills  off the family's youngest child gage it  was a big change that seemed to allow  the 