t from watching the film's  trailers and understanding that Mysterio  is traditionally a villain in the comics  to be truly surprised by a daring twist  you have to stick around until the mid  credit scene there it's revealed that  Mysterio doctored a video before his  death to make spider-man look like the  true villain of their struggle while  also outing Peter Parker as the man in  the mask this sudden change in the  character status quo plus the sudden  return of JK Simmons is Jay jonah  Jameson to the spider-man universe is  enough to make the audience feel as  shocked as Peter Parker set in 1969  Hollywood once upon a time in Hollywood  shows us a history of a tipping point  within both the film industry and Los  Angeles as a whole there's a sense of a  city and an art form on the brink and  Quentin Tarantino successfully creates  the feeling that anything might happen  then as the film reaches its climax he  drops the big twist it turns out that  anything can happen feeling is there to  set up Tarantino's dream version of  events a world in which Sharon Tate's  and her friends are never murdered by  the Manson Family and the family members  are instead bought off by clip booth and  Rick Dalton  Sharon survives Rick gets another shot  at a career and cliff is along for the  ride it's a bittersweet happily ever  after and one that lands even if you do  see it coming there are two major twists  in Joker and both are presented in a way  that creates a certain sense of  ambiguity so that you're not sure what  to believe the first arrives when it's  revealed that Arthur Fleck might  actually be the illegitimate son of  Swayne himself which makes him Bruce  Wayne's half-brother doubts is later  cast on this claim but Arthur seems to  cling to it and that attachment pays off  later the film's ending drops the second  major twist the riot arthur flack  inspired creates the environment in  which Bruce Wayne's parents were killed  so and the continuity of this movie the  Joker  inadvertently creates Batman does this  make the film too twisty for its own  good  your mileage may vary but there's no  doubt you left the theater thinking  about it  Shazam seemed to be a pretty traditional  superhero origin story as it follows  Billy Batson and his journey from orphan  boy to impossibly powerful superhero we  see Billy learning to use his new powers  in a mature way his connection to the  people who become his chosen family and  his eventual defeat to the supervillain  sivanna not just through brawn but  through the power of love the twist  comes in just how that love manifests  itself in the midst of his final battle  with sivanna Billy remembers the wizard  who gave him his powers hinted that he  would be able to share that power with  your heart unlock your greatest power  roams of our brothers and sisters await  Billy realizes that means that he must  pass his gifts on to his chosen family  and that's how in 2019 we got the Shazam  family on the big screen  the film's willingness to put such a  massive new development out there so  late in the story was part of what made  it so much fun one of the biggest keys  to parasite success is the way it lulls  you into thinking everything's going to  go one way before zipping off in another  unexpected direction the major turn  comes midway through the film just after  the Kim family has thoroughly  infiltrated the park family's lives at  this point director bong joon-ho has  expertly planted the seeds for what we  think is about to happen which is the  park family slow discovery that the Kim  family have calmed them then the  doorbell rings and the fired housekeeper  who we never expected to see again shows  up then she enters the park house again  and reveals both the secret bunker  beneath the structure and the man living  down there it's a brilliant turn that  subverts expectations and fits perfectly  within the film's framework knives out  provides ample opportunities for twists  and turns during its runtime and writer  director Rian Johnson delivers plenty  however the biggest plot twist at work  in knives out involves Harlan thrombi a  noted mystery writer who's found dead of  an apparent suicide at the beginning of  the film it's eventually revealed that  Farland did commit suicide after his  nurse Marta accidentally gave him what  she believed to be a fatal dose of  morphine Harlan killed himself  rather than risk Marta getting arrested  for a simple mistake but it turns out  there was even more to the story  in the end private investigator Benoit  Blanc reveals that Harlan's grandson  ransom actually switched the labels on  Harlan's medication to engineer the  morphine overdose but Martha gave Harlan  the right medication out of instinct so  the twist in the end is that there's not  a murder of any kind and that Harlan's  death really was just a misguided  suicide if you walk out of the  lighthouse and someone asks you what the  film's about so there's a good chance  you'll have some difficulty answering  that question yes it's the story of two  lighthouse keepers who seem to be slowly  losing their grip on sanity and reality  but if you really dig into the  intricacies of the film it's a lot more  complicated than that that said there's  still a powerful twist lying in wait  near the end of the film it comes when  the young wiki eeprom Winslet reveals  that his real name is Thomas Howard and  that Winslow was an identity he stole  from a man who died in a timber  accident that he didn't stop this  revelation and the guilt that comes with  it helps to add tremendous depth and  emotional weight to the film's powerful  climax plus there's the fact that the  twist means that both major characters  are named Thomas their similarities  contrasting against each other in  progressively more violent ways check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stop or coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube chan